{
  "name": "Chimney Forest",
  "stage": "Vents",
  "summary": "A field of black smokers. Each vent sits in a rock tube that is open only at the top, so heat and minerals rise as narrow jets and the alleys between chimneys stay cold and dark.",
  "pillars": [
    "Rock shapes the fields: a tube channels its plume upward, so food is in thin vertical jets, not in round halos.",
    "Feeding means hovering at a chimney mouth, at the edge of the burn line. A short dash in and out pays off; staying cooks the membrane.",
    "The cold lee below each chimney is a blind spot: lurkers wait there for cells that cut between tubes.",
    "Buoyant water rises (drift up), so the map reads bottom to top: start low and cold, the gate is high in the north-east."
  ],
  "proposals": [
    "Lurker behaviour: an ambush predator that stays still until a cell passes close, then lunges.",
    "Chimney growth: a tube adds a rock tile at its mouth over time and slowly chokes its own jet."
  ],
